===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|botel|t=bottle, flask, wineskin}}, from {{der|en|fro|boteille}} (Modern French {{m|fr|bouteille}}), from {{der|en|ML.|butticula}}, ultimately of disputed origin. Probably a diminutive of {{der|en|LL.|buttis}}. Compare also {{cog|nds|Buddel}} and {{cog|goh|būtil}} (whence {{cog|de|Beutel}}). {{doublet|en|botija}}.

Noun
{{en-noun}}

# A container, typically made of glass or plastic and having a tapered neck, used primarily for holding
#: {{m|en|Beer is often sold in '''bottles'''.}}
# The contents of such a container.
#: {{m|en|I only drank a '''bottle''' of beer.}}
# A container with a rubber nipple used for giving liquids to infants, a [[baby bottle]].
#: {{m|en|The baby wants a '''bottle'''.}}

