 “Fast Car” by several artists but originally by Chapman: 
“See, my old man’s got a problem […] '''bottle''' […] remember when we were driving […] his [the singer’s father’s] body’s too old for workin, his body’s too young to be lookin’ like [as worn and weathered as my father’s] his […] but somebody’s gotta [make money and] care for him [my father who was left to raise me, the singer, by himself] […] remember [toward the singer’s male partner] when we were driving—driving in your car [going] speeds so fast I [thought? FeltlikeIcould? ?] fly [or cry {depending on which perform:ance:er you pick to watch} I had a feeling that I belong; and I had a feeling [that] I [could be/am/will soon be] [proud of how I worked adamantly for my father, my boyfriend, and myself, so that we are all financially and otherwise unburdened with undue anxiety, stress, and worry: I’ll truly be able to be a] someone [for somebody I love {filial; romantic; self :: father, boyfriend, myself{man singing}]”

